WEBVTT

00:44.544 --> 00:49.716
DOONA!

01:07.776 --> 01:08.777
You're so heavy!

01:38.848 --> 01:40.975
- Hello.
- Hi.

01:41.059 --> 01:44.062
- These are all so pretty.
- Feel free to take a look.

01:49.234 --> 01:50.110
This one is pretty.

01:50.193 --> 01:51.027
- Is it?
- Yes.

01:51.111 --> 01:53.113
- We have a matching one for men.
- Do you?

01:54.906 --> 01:55.824
Try it on.

01:57.408 --> 01:58.368
Hurry and try it on.

01:59.327 --> 02:00.328
What do you think?

02:01.246 --> 02:02.872
- It's nice!
- It really is nice.

02:03.039 --> 02:04.499
EPISODE 8
TYPICAL AND ORDINARY

02:04.582 --> 02:06.251
- Shall we get them?
- Sounds good to me.

02:06.334 --> 02:10.380
You say

02:11.965 --> 02:17.303
That I'm always a genuine soul

02:19.848 --> 02:26.062
You also say

02:26.563 --> 02:29.983
That at least for today

02:30.066 --> 02:32.777
I am everyone's lover

02:34.821 --> 02:39.742
Tonight the clowns' farce wins applause

02:42.704 --> 02:47.500
As once again the fake masquerades as art

02:50.378 --> 02:53.089
Wear your leather…

02:53.173 --> 02:55.133
MOM

02:58.011 --> 03:03.141
Like a Hollywood movie star

03:10.648 --> 03:11.733
MOM

03:20.783 --> 03:25.997
I sometimes

03:27.874 --> 03:34.839
See myself in you

03:36.090 --> 03:42.180
One day

03:42.847 --> 03:43.681
My ugly…

03:43.765 --> 03:44.599
Right.

03:46.893 --> 03:49.812
If that's what the doctor said,
that's what we should do.

03:50.521 --> 03:54.609
If you've decided, don't put it off.
Ask them to schedule the surgery ASAP.

03:55.485 --> 03:56.361
Okay, bye.

04:02.158 --> 04:04.452
MINSONG NATIONAL UNIVERSITY
DEPARTMENT OF CLOTHING

04:07.121 --> 04:08.539
COME PICK ME UP
I'M TOO DRUNK TO WALK

04:08.623 --> 04:10.124
- Here's more.
- Put it over there.

04:10.208 --> 04:11.918
Well, I've sent it.

04:12.919 --> 04:17.382
It's going to be so embarrassing
if no one comes.

04:18.132 --> 04:20.176
Then that's just her fate.

04:23.012 --> 04:25.723
- To fate!
- To fate!

04:25.807 --> 04:26.724
Cheers!

04:41.447 --> 04:43.199
The fortune teller told me

04:43.283 --> 04:45.535
that I'm going to be
very lucky in love today.

04:45.618 --> 04:46.452
- Really?
- Yes.

04:46.536 --> 04:48.746
- I'm counting on you today.
- You can count on me.

04:50.915 --> 04:53.126
Come pick me up right now.

04:53.209 --> 04:55.336
I'm too drunk to walk.

04:59.007 --> 05:01.217
- Hey, I've got to go.
- What?

05:01.718 --> 05:03.678
- I have to go.
- Where are you going?

05:03.761 --> 05:04.679
What? Oh, I--

05:04.762 --> 05:06.180
- Wait.
- Let go! I have to go.

05:06.264 --> 05:08.891
- Where are you going?
- Look, I'll be back.

05:08.975 --> 05:10.268
- Yun-taek!
- Bye!

05:10.351 --> 05:12.353
Useless jerks, all of them.

05:19.819 --> 05:20.820
Someone's here.

05:22.447 --> 05:24.657
Hey, someone's here.

05:25.950 --> 05:29.037
Oh, fudge. It’s true.

05:30.872 --> 05:34.292
Hey, wake up.

05:34.375 --> 05:35.752
Wake up.

05:55.730 --> 05:58.816
We're home!

06:00.485 --> 06:02.278
We're home!

06:03.321 --> 06:04.572
Christ, I'm exhausted.

06:05.990 --> 06:07.617
No!

06:21.923 --> 06:23.341
What are you looking at?

06:23.424 --> 06:24.926
It’s making me want to kiss you.

06:39.607 --> 06:40.691
Damn it!

06:41.651 --> 06:44.404
Why did you dodge me?
Don't you know how to kiss?

06:44.487 --> 06:45.446
You're drunk.

06:45.530 --> 06:47.949
I'm stone sober now, thanks to you!

06:48.574 --> 06:50.284
- Are you sure?
- Yes, I'm sure!

06:58.793 --> 06:59.794
I like you too.

07:01.129 --> 07:02.713
I'm not the only one who's clueless.

07:07.635 --> 07:08.636
Wow.

07:10.638 --> 07:11.556
Shit.

07:12.598 --> 07:14.100
He's so damn hot.

07:47.842 --> 07:50.887
- You're so cute.
- You're so cute!

07:50.970 --> 07:53.473
Won-taek is kind of cute, like tofu.
Don't you think?

07:53.556 --> 07:55.975
Tofu! Won-taek, like tofu!

07:56.058 --> 08:00.521
- Stinky tofu! It's stinky tofu.
- Right? It's the color of stinky tofu!

08:00.605 --> 08:02.815
- So cute!
- It's Yun-taek, okay?

08:02.899 --> 08:04.358
- Won-taek!
- Won-taek!

08:04.442 --> 08:06.194
- Let's have a toast!
- Toast!

08:06.277 --> 08:08.237
Where's I-ra?

08:08.321 --> 08:11.115
Come on. Drink.

08:11.199 --> 08:12.867
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

08:15.244 --> 08:17.079
You drink so well!

08:17.163 --> 08:19.957
- That is good.
- But what's this? Isn't this a dimple?

08:20.041 --> 08:21.918
He even has dimples!

08:22.001 --> 08:24.420
- So cute!
- Your dimples are so cute!

08:24.504 --> 08:26.172
- Oh my!
- He's dressed so well too.

08:26.255 --> 08:27.715
Let's do this properly, then.

08:28.341 --> 08:31.761
- The stinky tofu is stripping.
- I'll pour you a drink!

08:31.844 --> 08:34.096
Love it!

08:34.180 --> 08:35.556
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

08:58.037 --> 09:04.043
You say

09:05.127 --> 09:10.716
That I'm always a genuine soul

09:13.302 --> 09:19.016
You also say

09:20.268 --> 09:23.396
That at least for today

09:23.479 --> 09:26.274
I am everyone's lover

09:28.401 --> 09:32.822
Tonight the clowns' farce wins applause

09:36.284 --> 09:37.118
As once again…

09:52.300 --> 09:56.012
Step, step, step, step, step

09:56.512 --> 09:59.849
Step, step, step, step, step…

10:17.950 --> 10:20.870
I just realized…

11:10.044 --> 11:12.588
Yay! It's the sea!

11:14.048 --> 11:15.341
It's right before us!

11:16.175 --> 11:17.093
So amazing.

11:17.176 --> 11:19.512
Be careful! You'll fall over at that rate.

11:32.692 --> 11:33.693
This is so nice.

11:35.986 --> 11:38.572
Honestly, your tastes are so predictable.

11:40.324 --> 11:41.867
I've always been that way.

11:42.493 --> 11:44.537
I like the most typical

11:45.830 --> 11:47.415
and ordinary things.

11:48.499 --> 11:49.750
It doesn't suit you.

12:06.475 --> 12:08.394
Don't you want to go back?

12:10.396 --> 12:12.189
- What?
- To what you were doing before.

12:13.607 --> 12:16.193
There must have been
some things you liked about it.

12:17.111 --> 12:18.404
You just lost sight of them.

12:23.409 --> 12:24.452
Would you let me go?

12:26.203 --> 12:29.582
What kind of question is that?
You should go if you want to.

12:31.667 --> 12:33.544
But I think it would be nice.

12:35.880 --> 12:37.506
I want to see you sing.

12:50.311 --> 12:52.438
I like that you're a fool.

12:58.360 --> 13:00.279
What if they tell me to break up with you?

13:01.197 --> 13:02.281
Should I still go back?

13:12.958 --> 13:14.335
Hello?

13:14.418 --> 13:16.253
Your voice is a bit hoarse.

13:17.379 --> 13:20.049
- Are you having a rough time?
- Yes.

13:23.093 --> 13:26.388
I only got here a few days ago,
and I miss you already.

13:28.015 --> 13:29.016
Me too.

13:33.896 --> 13:35.314
Is it raining there too?

13:37.817 --> 13:41.028
No. It's overcast,
but it's not raining yet.

13:50.788 --> 13:53.082
Apparently,
it's going to rain a lot this year.

14:47.428 --> 14:49.763
I SAW MY LOVE DOONA
AT THE NERD CONNECTION'S CONCERT

14:49.847 --> 14:51.223
DOONA THE GODDESS! BEAUTIFUL!

14:51.307 --> 14:54.518
Lee Doona!

14:54.685 --> 14:56.645
LEE DOONA MADE A SURPRISE APPEARANCE

14:56.729 --> 14:59.273
Lee Doona!

15:33.515 --> 15:34.350
CERTIFIED MAIL

15:34.433 --> 15:37.770
LAWSUIT NOTICE FOR DAMAGES CLAIM
RELATED TO BREACH OF CONTRACT

15:37.853 --> 15:41.440
Hello. I am Jung Ji-guk,the legal
representative of MSA Entertainment.

15:41.523 --> 15:45.569
My client has started proceedings
against you for financial damages.

15:47.071 --> 15:49.698
I believe you’ve received
the certified mail.

15:50.366 --> 15:54.036
From this point on, I would prefer
to speak with your legal representative.

16:38.247 --> 16:41.750
LAWSUIT NOTICE FOR DAMAGES CLAIM
RELATED TO BREACH OF CONTRACT

16:41.834 --> 16:45.212
YOU HAVE INCURRED A PENALTY
DUE TO YOUR UNILATERAL BREACH OF CONTRACT

16:57.891 --> 16:59.226
Don't smoke in here.

17:07.943 --> 17:09.611
Did you really have to go this far?

17:13.073 --> 17:14.450
You think it was me?

17:21.206 --> 17:22.666
I wouldn't have stopped at this.

17:22.750 --> 17:25.169
We agreed to terminate the contract
on the condition

17:25.252 --> 17:27.296
that I did not sign with another agency.

17:32.468 --> 17:34.386
Did you think that would be possible?

17:35.095 --> 17:36.638
I may have washed my hands of you,

17:37.681 --> 17:39.600
but I can't stop Ms. Ma's actions.

17:42.686 --> 17:46.482
You've set a bad example in the industry.
No company would let you off the hook.

17:50.235 --> 17:51.320
And if they don't?

17:51.820 --> 17:53.322
Irrespective of the compensation,

17:53.405 --> 17:56.325
they'll drag the trial out
for as long as possible to torment you

17:56.408 --> 17:59.787
and destroy your public image
with an endless smear campaign

17:59.870 --> 18:01.371
with no regard for the truth.

18:01.997 --> 18:03.332
A comeback after that?

18:04.958 --> 18:06.543
You couldn't even if you wanted to.

18:19.264 --> 18:21.225
Just tell me what I need to do.

18:21.892 --> 18:25.395
Don't you already know
that this is your chance?

18:26.230 --> 18:28.649
I've taken care of the videos
that were posted online.

18:28.732 --> 18:31.151
For your part, get rid of that boy first.

18:32.069 --> 18:35.155
If you do make a comeback,
they'll rip you to shreds because of him.

18:40.661 --> 18:43.163
- Have you got everything?
- Of course! I have everything.

18:43.247 --> 18:44.081
Me too.

18:44.164 --> 18:46.208
- We have enough, right?
- Of course!

18:46.291 --> 18:48.752
- Yes, definitely!
- Here, left pocket.

18:50.462 --> 18:51.296
Got it.

18:55.384 --> 18:57.594
Stop right there. What's that ring?

18:57.678 --> 18:59.179
Do you have a girlfriend?

18:59.680 --> 19:02.933
- Took you long enough to notice!
- I know! Is she pretty?

19:03.016 --> 19:05.144
- Yes.
- Asshole! What about me, man?

19:05.227 --> 19:07.187
- I want to meet her.
- All right, soon.

19:07.271 --> 19:09.982
Tell me how I can meet a pretty girl.

19:15.237 --> 19:17.114
Won-yeong is being discharged on Sunday.

19:17.197 --> 19:19.867
I'll come up straight after,
even if it ends up being late.

19:20.701 --> 19:22.202
Oh, I have to go.

19:23.162 --> 19:25.581
- Okay, then.
- I'll call you.

19:42.139 --> 19:43.557
I'm off to Na-yeong's.

19:43.640 --> 19:45.893
Okay. Oh! Take this.

19:47.144 --> 19:48.103
It's from Doona.

19:49.438 --> 19:50.480
Thank you.

19:51.773 --> 19:53.358
- See you later.
- Bye.

19:58.363 --> 20:00.616
You really didn't have to bring anything.

20:01.491 --> 20:03.785
- So you're taking time off school.
- Yes.

20:04.286 --> 20:07.164
I've cut ties with my dad,
so I can't afford the fees.

20:07.664 --> 20:09.875
And you and Won-jun are
such eyesores to me.

20:09.958 --> 20:11.251
There are multiple reasons.

20:11.793 --> 20:13.879
You don't have to be quite so honest.

20:15.505 --> 20:17.758
I got a job at a cram school.
I'll treat you sometime.

20:20.469 --> 20:22.721
I guess you don't hate me that much, then?

20:25.849 --> 20:28.602
My dad has run
in three National Assembly elections

20:28.685 --> 20:30.687
and failed to get elected all three times.

20:30.771 --> 20:34.650
And every time it happens,
he loves to bad-mouth the winner.

20:34.733 --> 20:37.903
I mean, how is that the winner’s fault?

20:39.238 --> 20:41.031
Tripping yourself up

20:41.114 --> 20:44.409
and then blaming someone else
makes you look so pathetic.

20:47.621 --> 20:51.124
I have to say,
your dad really is obnoxious.

20:53.752 --> 20:58.090
On the night of the Start of Term Party,
I answered his call.

20:59.341 --> 21:01.385
- Hello?
- You crazy bitch.

21:02.052 --> 21:05.222
What kind of scum
are you out with at this time of night?

21:07.432 --> 21:08.600
No way!

21:09.559 --> 21:11.103
I had no idea!

21:14.815 --> 21:17.985
I started to warm up to you
from that point on.

21:18.902 --> 21:22.447
And I felt for you that you were trying
so hard to appear perfect.

21:25.242 --> 21:26.702
That's so embarrassing.

21:26.785 --> 21:29.288
There's nothing
to be embarrassed about between friends.

21:29.371 --> 21:31.081
I've been living life all wrong.

21:31.748 --> 21:33.875
It's not like pretending changes anything.

21:36.128 --> 21:39.798
There are people
who live their lives wrong, but not you.

21:46.722 --> 21:48.640
Why did you come over, by the way?

21:51.351 --> 21:52.311
I missed you.

21:54.271 --> 21:55.856
I told you I liked you.

24:30.343 --> 24:34.598
NOWDROWZ
INSOMNIA, NON-HABIT-FORMING, SLEEP AID

25:18.725 --> 25:19.726
You're up.

25:19.809 --> 25:21.144
Want some coffee?

25:22.604 --> 25:23.522
Sure.

25:24.022 --> 25:25.440
I'll make toast.

26:29.921 --> 26:32.424
Talk. You're here
because you have something to say.

26:32.507 --> 26:35.302
Do you still have
business left with Doona?

26:37.304 --> 26:40.932
Because I'd like you to stop visiting her
in a personal capacity and harassing her.

26:43.184 --> 26:44.769
Why are you so angry?

26:45.854 --> 26:49.608
How old are you? 21? 22?
Have you completed military service?

26:50.317 --> 26:52.694
By the time you've done that,
graduated, got a job,

26:52.777 --> 26:54.946
and whatever else,
it'll be five years from now.

26:57.157 --> 26:58.450
Will you date her until then?

26:59.868 --> 27:01.661
- Realistically--
- I don't see why not.

27:04.623 --> 27:05.457
Sure.

27:06.541 --> 27:09.419
There are also people in this world
who believe in things

27:09.502 --> 27:12.631
like fairies, ghosts,
and past life connections.

27:13.673 --> 27:15.091
A kid like you could think that.

27:15.175 --> 27:17.552
Then why don't you
leave us kids alone to play?

27:17.636 --> 27:20.555
Because there is too much at stake
to let you do that.

27:21.264 --> 27:22.223
Don't exaggerate.

27:26.144 --> 27:27.187
Is that what you think?

27:28.647 --> 27:30.690
In an industry
where public image is everything,

27:30.774 --> 27:33.943
bringing her back after she messed up
and cut out is a huge risk.

27:34.027 --> 27:37.864
Public opinion is at rock bottom,
and no one can predict what will happen.

27:38.365 --> 27:40.533
If the profit expected
from Doona is ten billion,

27:40.617 --> 27:42.994
the potential loss
we have to take on is even higher.

27:43.078 --> 27:47.165
Given all this, neither the company
nor Doona is stupid enough

27:47.248 --> 27:49.501
to take on the risk of a relationship.

27:52.504 --> 27:55.632
So, who should be
the one to let her go? Me?

29:18.548 --> 29:22.886
I think Doona's had a lot to think about,
and what she wanted from the company was

29:23.803 --> 29:28.433
to give her a bit more say
in her work going forward.

29:28.516 --> 29:29.809
Oh, of course!

29:29.893 --> 29:32.771
She should have a say
and create the kind of music she wants.

29:32.854 --> 29:34.981
From now on,
the company will reduce involvement

29:35.064 --> 29:37.692
and let Doona dictate the direction
she wants to take.

29:37.776 --> 29:40.069
Why would we interfere?

29:40.153 --> 29:41.780
Of course we mustn't.

29:41.863 --> 29:45.283
Our job is to allow the artist
to do what they want.

29:45.366 --> 29:48.453
Doona, please feel free to do
what you want. We won't interfere.

29:48.536 --> 29:50.371
Make the kind of music you want.

29:50.955 --> 29:53.583
How many tracks
did you say are in the works?

29:54.334 --> 29:58.338
We have about five or six
from artists that Doona selected.

30:01.674 --> 30:04.385
If there's anything you need right away,
just ask Mr. Ko.

30:05.136 --> 30:07.806
I'll take care of the move,
so don't worry about it.

30:08.556 --> 30:10.683
Just tell me anything specific
that you need.

30:13.228 --> 30:17.190
Isn't it amazing that I've suddenly
regained my ability to sing?

30:17.941 --> 30:19.609
I find it amazing.

30:22.821 --> 30:24.072
How can I let go?

30:25.281 --> 30:29.452
You're good at discarding people,
so you tell me

30:30.119 --> 30:31.663
what it is I need to do…

30:33.873 --> 30:35.917
to let go of him.

30:37.335 --> 30:39.045
Because I don't think I can do it.

30:42.632 --> 30:43.758
I'll do a good job.

30:45.009 --> 30:48.513
I'll succeed enough to justify the time
and money that's been invested in me.

30:49.722 --> 30:52.267
Enough for them to forget
about the company's losses.

30:52.350 --> 30:55.311
I'm not doing this because of the lawsuit.

30:55.395 --> 30:56.855
And it's nothing to do with you.

30:57.522 --> 30:58.398
I know.

30:59.482 --> 31:01.568
I realized I wanted to be happy.

31:02.318 --> 31:03.152
So…

31:14.789 --> 31:15.915
I met him.

31:17.041 --> 31:19.419
He came to see me. Didn't he tell you?

31:21.004 --> 31:23.715
For now, cut contact with everyone.
This is not a request.

31:24.757 --> 31:27.093
Rest up. Things are going to
get busy from tomorrow.

31:27.927 --> 31:29.387
What did you say to him?

31:35.435 --> 31:36.644
There wasn't much to say.

31:37.770 --> 31:39.188
What could I say to a kid?

31:48.406 --> 31:53.202
Like a Hollywood movie star

32:03.671 --> 32:06.007
Thank you, everybody.

32:06.090 --> 32:09.385
Today's performance has been
particularly nerve-racking for me,

32:09.469 --> 32:12.889
and the reason is
that I spotted a familiar face

32:12.972 --> 32:15.725
in the audience earlier this evening.

32:15.808 --> 32:18.311
I'm a huge fan of hers.

32:18.394 --> 32:21.689
Dream Sweet's Ms. Lee Doona.

32:21.773 --> 32:23.566
What? Dream Sweet's Lee Doona?

32:24.692 --> 32:25.902
I'm right, aren't I?

32:28.529 --> 32:32.492
Would it be okay
if I invited you to join me on stage?

32:36.579 --> 32:40.959
Lee Doona!

32:41.042 --> 32:45.463
Lee Doona!

32:45.546 --> 32:49.717
Lee Doona!

33:07.694 --> 33:08.611
You're so cool!

33:13.032 --> 33:17.203
If you don't mind,
may I ask you to sing something for us?

33:51.529 --> 33:54.490
I just realized

33:56.826 --> 33:59.912
The endless winter

34:03.374 --> 34:07.587
And the maze that is my heart

34:46.125 --> 34:48.836
I just realized

34:48.920 --> 34:51.839
The endless winter

34:52.590 --> 34:56.010
And the maze that is my heart

34:56.094 --> 34:58.221
All that time I spent suffering

34:58.304 --> 35:01.224
Pierced by the thorns…

37:26.702 --> 37:29.038
I just realized

37:29.538 --> 37:32.250
The endless winter

37:33.125 --> 37:36.587
And the maze that is my heart

37:36.671 --> 37:39.173
All that time I spent suffering

37:39.257 --> 37:44.804
Pierced by the thorns

37:45.429 --> 37:47.098
With love

37:47.181 --> 37:52.728
Every day felt as heavy as lead

37:52.812 --> 37:54.981
Days passed by

37:55.064 --> 37:57.858
Where I didn't expect
Anything good to happen

37:57.942 --> 38:04.699
And you, a total stranger, came to me

38:05.408 --> 38:08.786
You were a whole other universe

38:10.496 --> 38:15.167
I was a fool back then

38:15.251 --> 38:17.003
Trapped in fear

38:17.086 --> 38:20.214
I didn't understand anything about myself

38:20.298 --> 38:25.303
I now realize that my dream is

38:25.386 --> 38:29.849
To spend an ordinary day
Walking by your side

38:30.641 --> 38:35.354
I still remember the day

38:35.438 --> 38:38.149
How you embraced my heart

38:38.232 --> 38:40.901
And how my heart fluttered

38:40.985 --> 38:45.031
I still remember the day

38:45.531 --> 38:50.244
I want to tell you these words now

38:50.328 --> 38:52.955
Stay with me

38:55.041 --> 38:57.668
I just realized

38:57.752 --> 39:00.546
Taking my shaky first steps

39:01.422 --> 39:04.633
I took another step

39:05.134 --> 39:07.470
Held your hand

39:07.970 --> 39:12.683
And smiled so wide

39:14.060 --> 39:15.186
With love

39:15.269 --> 39:20.232
I dug up my feelings for you
And my confusing thoughts

39:20.316 --> 39:23.486
That had been buried deep within

39:23.569 --> 39:27.031
And entrusted them to you

39:28.741 --> 39:33.496
I was a fool back then

39:33.579 --> 39:35.331
Trapped in fear

39:35.414 --> 39:38.501
I didn't understand anything about myself

39:38.584 --> 39:43.589
I now realize that my dream is

39:43.672 --> 39:48.219
To spend an ordinary day
Walking by your side

39:48.928 --> 39:53.599
I still remember the day

39:53.682 --> 39:56.310
How you embraced my heart

39:56.394 --> 39:59.063
And how my heart fluttered

39:59.146 --> 40:03.734
I still remember the day

40:03.818 --> 40:08.572
I want to tell you these words now

40:08.656 --> 40:10.533
Stay with me

40:10.616 --> 40:12.410
Subtitle translation by: Reuben Simpson
